=========================================================
CLASS TEMPLATES (Interview Revision)
=========================================================

What is a Class Template?
-------------------------
A class template allows writing one generic class that works with multiple
data types.

Syntax

template<typename T>
class Box
{
    T value;

public:
    Box(T v) : value(v) {}

    T getValue() const
    {
        return value;
    }
};

Usage

Box<int> b1(10);
Box<double> b2(3.14);
Box<string> b3("Hello");

---------------------------------------------------------

Template Instantiation
----------------------

A class template is a blueprint.

The compiler generates the required class only when it is instantiated.

Example

Box<int>      -> Generates Box<int>

Box<double>   -> Generates Box<double>

---------------------------------------------------------

Multiple Template Parameters
----------------------------

template<typename T, typename U>
class Pair
{
    T first;
    U second;
};

Pair<int,string> p;

---------------------------------------------------------

Member Function Outside Class
-----------------------------

template<typename T>
T Box<T>::getValue()
{
    return value;
}

Always use

ClassName<T>::

---------------------------------------------------------

Default Template Arguments
--------------------------

template<typename T = int>
class Box
{
};

Box<> b;      // Box<int>

---------------------------------------------------------

Non-Type Template Parameters
----------------------------

template<typename T, int SIZE>
class Array
{
    T data[SIZE];
};

Array<int,10> arr;

---------------------------------------------------------

Static Members
--------------

Each template instantiation has its own static member.

Counter<int>::count

Counter<double>::count

are different variables.

---------------------------------------------------------

Header Files
------------

Template definitions are usually placed in .h/.hpp files because the compiler
must see the complete definition during template instantiation.

---------------------------------------------------------

Common STL Class Templates
--------------------------

vector<T>

list<T>

map<Key,Value>

pair<T,U>

queue<T>

stack<T>

---------------------------------------------------------

Interview Questions
-------------------

Q. What is a class template?
A generic class that works with multiple data types.

Q. Difference between function template and class template?

Function Template
• Generates functions
• Type usually deduced

Class Template
• Generates classes
• Type usually specified explicitly

Q. What is template instantiation?
Compiler generates the actual class from the template.

Q. Why are template definitions kept in header files?
The compiler needs the complete definition during instantiation.

Q. Can class templates have multiple template parameters?
Yes.

Q. Can class templates have static members?
Yes. Each template instantiation gets its own copy.

